### Rotating Card (Hover Effect)

Below is a minimal example that shows how to create a card that rotates around its center when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an HTML file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;   /* center horizontally */
    align-items: center;       /* center vertically */
    height: 100vh;             /* full viewport height */
    background: #f0f0f0;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;      /* give depth to 3D transform */
}

.card {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
    color: #fff;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* rotate 180° around Y axis */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Optional: back side styling ---------- */
.card::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: #333;
    color: #fff;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.6s ease;
    backface-visibility: hidden;     /* hide backside during rotation */
}

.card:hover::after {
    opacity: 1;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <h2>Front Side</h2>
        <p>Hover over me!</p>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on `.card-wrapper` | Gives a 3D depth effect so the rotation looks realistic. |
| **2** | `.card` styles | Sets size, background, shadow, and enables 3D transforms with `transform-style: preserve-3d`. |
| **3** | `transition` + `transform` on hover | Smoothly rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis when hovered. |
| **4** | `::after` pseudo‑element | Creates a “back” side that appears after the rotation. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides it until the card is flipped. |

Feel free to replace the gradient, text, or add more content inside the card. If you want a different axis (X, Z) or a different angle, just change the `rotateY(180deg)` to something like `rotateX(180deg)` or `rotateZ(360deg)`.

Happy coding!
